WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:01:04.879 --> 00:01:08.880
To give you an idea of just how quickly

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.560
Lebanon is collapsing, you have to

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:13.280
realize that it's even worse than

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:15.439
Venezuela - a poster child of devastated

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:18.000
economies. 

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:22.080
After years

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:24.320
of corruption, mismanagement and

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:26.479
dysfunctional politics, Lebanon's dealing

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:28.320
with a huge currency crisis,

00:01:26.479 --> 00:01:31.200
and that's at the root of so many other

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:31.200
problems right now.

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:45.280
So

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:47.360
here's what's going on. In the late 1990s

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:49.680
the Lebanese pound was pegged to the U.S.

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:52.159
dollar. The exchange rate was fixed at

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:54.320
1500 pounds for one dollar. Now the

00:01:52.159 --> 00:01:56.399
problem with that is Lebanon's economy

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:58.960
wasn't strong enough to really justify

00:01:56.399 --> 00:02:00.719
that value. It was sort of artificial. For

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:02.479
a long time, the government and banks

00:02:00.719 --> 00:02:04.640
managed to prop up the currency to

00:02:02.479 --> 00:02:06.159
maintain that peg. But now, they're at a

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:08.800
point where they just can't do that

00:02:06.159 --> 00:02:10.879
anymore. And so the currency has crashed,

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:13.520
losing up to 90 percent of its value in

00:02:10.879 --> 00:02:15.840
the last two years. And that means

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:17.040
people's savings and salaries have

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:18.720
tanked.

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:30.160
If your currency is worth less, it

00:02:28.319 --> 00:02:32.800
makes importing things much more

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:34.319
expensive. For Lebanon, that's a massive

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:37.519
deal because it imports nearly

00:02:34.319 --> 00:02:39.840
everything. Including all its fuel. So now

00:02:37.519 --> 00:02:42.640
on top of the currency crisis, there's a

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:42.640
fuel crisis.

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:47.440
The government simply can't afford to

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:49.440
buy enough and it's abandoned some of

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:51.840
the fuel subsidies that helped make fuel

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:54.239
affordable for ordinary people. So now

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:56.720
you've got both shortages, and super high

00:02:54.239 --> 00:02:56.720
prices.

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:17.760
So the fuel crisis is creating a domino

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:20.640
Effect. Drinking water now costs four

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:22.640
times what it used to, and the lights are

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:24.319
literally going out because there's no

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:26.080
fuel for generators. 

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:41.920
So

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:44.640
it only gets worse - because now you've

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:47.360
got a health crisis too. Hospitals are

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:49.680
struggling, the U.N. has got involved - even

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:52.480
supplying fuel to help keep generators

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:55.200
running. And like other imports, medicine

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:57.840
has become too expensive or hard to find.

00:03:55.200 --> 00:04:00.560
Even ordinary drugs like paracetamol, let

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:02.159
alone life-saving ones for diabetics or

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:04.560
cancer patients.

00:04:02.159 --> 00:04:06.239
So people like marina are stepping in.

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:08.640
She set up a charity to coordinate

00:04:06.239 --> 00:04:11.040
donations of medicine from abroad. 

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:27.120
That idea that the state is missing in

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:29.680
action, well that's why things have

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:31.360
become so desperate. 

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:47.280
And this isn't

00:04:44.639 --> 00:04:50.080
exactly new. It's almost as if Lebanon is

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:52.000
in a permanent state of political crisis,

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:53.840
and critics say part of the problem is

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:55.680
the system itself.

00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:57.280
Now the way it works is that the three

00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:59.440
biggest sects are guaranteed

00:04:57.280 --> 00:05:01.840
representation. That was the deal to keep

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:03.680
the peace after the civil war. So for

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:05.520
example, the president is always a

00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:07.039
Maronite Christian, the prime minister is

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:09.440
always Sunni and the speaker of

00:05:07.039 --> 00:05:12.320
parliament is Shia. But in reality it's

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:14.720
led to political gridlock, infighting and

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:16.720
nothing really gets done. 

00:05:38.639 --> 00:05:42.560
You end up with a lot of

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:44.479
corruption and accusations that

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:46.560
politicians are only serving their own

00:05:44.479 --> 00:05:49.639
interests, not working for the good of

00:05:46.560 --> 00:05:49.639
the country.

00:05:55.759 --> 00:05:59.680
A couple of years ago, hundreds of

00:05:57.440 --> 00:06:02.680
thousands of people protested to say as

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:02.680
much.

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:15.360
And after the horrific explosion in

00:06:13.199 --> 00:06:17.759
Beirut last year, there was outrage

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:21.560
directed at politicians. And so far no

00:06:17.759 --> 00:06:21.560
one's been held to account.

00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:40.000
What's happened recently, is that the

00:06:37.759 --> 00:06:42.400
political parties have finally agreed on

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:44.560
a new government after 13 months.

00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:56.479
Like billionaire Prime Minister,

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:58.880
Najib Mikati - who's had the job twice

00:06:56.479 --> 00:06:58.880
already.

00:07:07.199 --> 00:07:12.000
He's trying to manage expectations, but

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:13.919
they're already rock bottom. 

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:35.680
And there's a

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:37.840
lot that needs doing. Priority number one,

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:39.759
is to get cash into the country. And the

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:42.319
government's best bet is to secure a

00:07:39.759 --> 00:07:44.400
bailout from the IMF. It's now planning

00:07:42.319 --> 00:07:46.720
to reopen talks with them after the last

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:48.879
ones stalled in 2020. But if the

00:07:46.720 --> 00:07:51.199
government wants money, it will also need

00:07:48.879 --> 00:07:53.840
to present a recovery plan that includes

00:07:51.199 --> 00:07:56.240
a bunch of reforms. 

00:08:10.879 --> 00:08:14.800
If there's any chance of that happening,

00:08:13.360 --> 00:08:17.039
it could start with parliamentary

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:18.319
elections coming up in May. But that's a

00:08:17.039 --> 00:08:20.319
big if.

00:08:18.319 --> 00:08:22.080
Just like fuel and medicine,

00:08:20.319 --> 00:08:24.319
hope that politicians will actually

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:26.879
change things is in seriously short

00:08:24.319 --> 00:08:28.639
supply.

